<title>USA: Freddie Mac says credit losses decline.</title>
<headline>Freddie Mac says credit losses decline.</headline>
<dateline>MACLEAN, Va. 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federal Home Mortgage (Freddie Mac) said Tuesday its credit losses relative to its portfolio declined to the lowest level in two years.</p>
<p>The company said this was the result of continuing improvements in mortgage and underwriting services.</p>
<p>David Glenn, president and chief operating officer, said &quot;...in an environment of generally tight financial spreads, we produced strong retained portfolio growth through sharp execution in purchasing assets and issuing debt.&quot;</p>
</text>
